SlopOS handoff diagnostics for Limine 12.9.1

SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-2-Clause
A derivative of Limine (BSD-2-Clause, see COPYING in its tree), not part of
upstream Limine. Applies to the tree of the limine-12.9.1 release tarball with
`patch -p1` or `git apply`; scripts/build_limine_diag.sh applies it and builds.
README.md beside this file says how to read what it draws.

From fb_init to common_spinup it draws into framebuffer 0: a trail of the
steps reached, a report of any CPU exception (vectors 0-31, through an IDT it
installs right after fb_init and one with Limine's code selector after
common_spinup's GDT switch), and a report of any page Limine handed out that
changed behind its back (per-page checksums verified after ExitBootServices,
after build_pagemap, after init_smp and before common_spinup, plus the kernel
image against its ELF file). It never calls Limine's allocator: its tables live
in pages the firmware hands out at boot(), and the build pads the image to the
stock binary's size, because firmware places a loader by its size and every
Limine allocation moves with it. The PNG/JPEG/BMP wallpaper decoder is dropped
to make the room.

Compile-time options, through CPPFLAGS_FOR_TARGET:
  -DSLOPOS_DIAG_TEST_FAULT=<n>    take a #GP when step kind n starts
                                  (kinds in common/lib/slopos_diag.h)
  -DSLOPOS_DIAG_TEST_CORRUPT=<n>  flip a word Limine owns: 1 the requests array
                                  and 2 the kernel image at the EBS check, 3 a
                                  page-table page at the SMP check, 4 the
                                  kernel image before anything is sealed
  -DSLOPOS_DIAG_E9_TRACE          every allocation on port 0xe9 (QEMU debugcon)
  -DSLOPOS_DIAG_STOCK_IMAGE_SIZE, -DSLOPOS_DIAG_PAD_RODATA,
  -DSLOPOS_DIAG_PAD_BSS           set by the build script

